# Packaging completeness for the shipped test suite.
#
# The sdist includes `tests/*.py` (setuptools picks them up), which meant an
# unpacked sdist shipped test files whose inputs it did not carry: no conftest,
# no `tests/fixtures/*.wasm`. Running `pytest` there produced dozens of failures
# that looked like product regressions and were packaging gaps.
#
# So: ship what the shipped tests need. Modules that inspect REPOSITORY files
# (project metadata, scripts, module sources) are skipped with an explicit reason
# when those files are absent — see `tests/conftest.py`. Nothing is skipped in a
# real checkout, so CI keeps every gate.

include tests/conftest.py
include tests/fixtures/*.wasm
include tests/fixtures/*.wat
